Let the region $z<0$ be composed of a uniform dielectric material for which $\epsilon_{R1}=3.2 , while$ the region $z>0$ is characterized by $\epsilon_{R2}=2$. Let $D_1=-30a_x+50a_y+70a_z\text{ nC/m}^2$ and find:-
(a) $D_{t1}$ (Tangential component of $D$ in Region 1);
(b) Polarization ($P_1$);
(c) $E_{$n^2$}$ (Normal component of $E$ in Region 2)
(d) $E_{t2}$ (Tangential component of $E$ in Region 2)

An EM wave travels in free space with the electric field component $\vec{E} = (15\mathbf{a}_y - 5\mathbf{a}_x) \cos(\omega t - 3y + 5z)\text{V/m}$. Find;
(a) $\omega$ and $\lambda$.
(b) The magnetic field component.

Let the region $z<0$ be composed of a uniform dielectric material for which $\epsilon_{R1}=3.2 , while$ the region $z>0$ is characterized by $\epsilon_{R2}=2$. Let $\mathbf{D_1}=-30\mathbf{a_x}+50\mathbf{a_y}+70\mathbf{a_z}\text{ nC/m}^2$ and find:-
(a) $\mathbf{D_{t1}}$ (Tangential component of $\mathbf{D}$ in Region 1);
(b) Polarization ($\mathbf{P_1}$);
(c) $\mathbf{E_{$n^2$}}$ (Normal component of $\mathbf{E}$ in Region 2)
(d) $\mathbf{E_{t2}}$ (Tangential component of $\mathbf{E}$ in Region 2)
